# LLM Gateway - .NET 8 Project Rules

You are an expert .NET developer building an enterprise-grade LLM Gateway proxy service. This application intercepts LLM API requests, sanitizes sensitive data, and provides audit logging for compliance.

## Project Overview

- **Framework**: .NET 8 (latest LTS)
- **Architecture**: Clean Architecture with vertical slices
- **Primary Language**: C# 12
- **Testing**: xUnit with FluentAssertions and NSubstitute
- **Database**: PostgreSQL with Entity Framework Core
- **Cache**: Redis (StackExchange.Redis)
- **Observability**: OpenTelemetry, Serilog

## Code Style & Conventions

### C# Coding Standards

```csharp
// Use file-scoped namespaces
namespace LLMGateway.Core.Services;

// Use primary constructors for DI
public class SanitizationService(
    IMappingManager mappingManager,
    IRuleRegistry ruleRegistry,
    ILogger<SanitizationService> logger) : ISanitizationService
{
    public async Task<SanitizationResult> SanitizeAsync(string content, Session session)
    {
        // Implementation
    }
}

// Prefer records for DTOs and immutable types
public record SanitizationResult(
    string SanitizedContent,
    bool WasSanitized,
    IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string> Mappings);

// Use init-only properties for configuration
public class GatewayOptions
{
    public required int Port { get; init; }
    public required bool EnableTls { get; init; }
    public TimeSpan SessionTimeout { get; init; } = TimeSpan.FromHours(8);
}
```

### Naming Conventions

- **Interfaces**: `IServiceName` (e.g., `ISanitizationEngine`)
- **Async methods**: Suffix with `Async` (e.g., `ProcessRequestAsync`)
- **Private fields**: `_camelCase` with underscore prefix
- **Constants**: `PascalCase` (not SCREAMING_CASE)
- **Extension methods**: In `Extensions` namespace, class named `{Type}Extensions`

### File Organization

```
src/
├── LLMGateway.Api/              # ASP.NET Core Web API
│   ├── Controllers/
│   ├── Middleware/
│   ├── Filters/
│   └── Program.cs
├── LLMGateway.Core/             # Domain logic (no external dependencies)
│   ├── Entities/
│   ├── Interfaces/
│   ├── Services/
│   └── Exceptions/
├── LLMGateway.Infrastructure/    # External concerns
│   ├── Persistence/
│   ├── Redis/
│   ├── Encryption/
│   └── LlmProviders/
└── LLMGateway.Proxy/            # HTTP Proxy implementation
    ├── Handlers/
    └── Certificates/
tests/
├── LLMGateway.UnitTests/
├── LLMGateway.IntegrationTests/
└── LLMGateway.ArchitectureTests/
```

## Architecture Patterns

### Dependency Injection

```csharp
// Register services in extension methods
public static class ServiceCollectionExtensions
{
    public static IServiceCollection AddSanitizationServices(
        this IServiceCollection services,
        IConfiguration configuration)
    {
        services.Configure<SanitizationOptions>(
            configuration.GetSection("Sanitization"));
        
        services.AddSingleton<IRuleRegistry, RuleRegistry>();
        services.AddScoped<ISanitizationEngine, SanitizationEngine>();
        services.AddScoped<IComplianceDetector, ComplianceDetector>();
        
        return services;
    }
}
```

### Result Pattern (No Exceptions for Flow Control)

```csharp
// Use Result<T> for operations that can fail
public readonly record struct Result<T>
{
    public T? Value { get; }
    public string? Error { get; }
    public bool IsSuccess => Error is null;
    
    public static Result<T> Success(T value) => new() { Value = value };
    public static Result<T> Failure(string error) => new() { Error = error };
}

// Usage
public async Task<Result<ProxyResponse>> ProcessAsync(ProxyRequest request)
{
    var policyResult = await _policyEngine.EvaluateAsync(request.UserId);
    if (!policyResult.IsSuccess)
        return Result<ProxyResponse>.Failure(policyResult.Error);
    
    // Continue processing...
}
```

